{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-181759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in N:3n-5\\le -4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $3n-5\\le -4.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-5 & \\le -4 \\\\ 3n & \\le 1 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, no natural number satisfies the inequality above. So, we conclude that the set\n$A$ contains no elements. Hence, $A=∅.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cfaa5b9d30900903e28e1bba97790ae61bb22126fc0e2fa27da8250a38beaca9"} {"question" "q-181759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "N"] ["math" "{1,2,3}"] ["math" "{1,2}"] ["math" "{\\pm 1,\\pm 2}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-180759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in Z:5n+25=10}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-180759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the equation $5n+25=10.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our equation for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n+25 & =10 \\\\ 5n & =-15 \\\\ n & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is $n=-3,$ which is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={-3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-180759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cfaa5b9d30900903e28e1bba97790ae61bb22126fc0e2fa27da8250a38beaca9"} {"question" "q-180759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cour