on $4n+7=-9.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our equation for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4n+7 & =-9 \\\\ 4n & =-16 \\\\ n & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $-4\\notin N,$ we conclude that the set $A$ contains no elements. Hence, $A=∅.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cfaa5b9d30900903e28e1bba97790ae61bb22126fc0e2fa27da8250a38beaca9"} {"question" "q-181755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "N"] ["math" "Z"] ["math" "{-4}"] ["math" "{4}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-180766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which set is equivalent to $B={n\\in Z:2n-11<-4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-180766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $2n-11<-4.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n-11 & <-4 \\\\ 2n & <7 \\\\ n & <\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $3,2,1,0,-1,-2,….$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nB={…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-180766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cfaa5b9d30900903e28e1bba97790ae61bb22126fc0e2fa27da8250a38beaca9"} {"question" "q-180766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-180766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{-2,-1,0,1,2,3}"] ["math" "{0,1,2,3}"] ["math" "{…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}"] ["math" "{…,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2}"] ["math" "{…,-4,-3,-2,-1,0}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-180766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in N:2{n}^{2}-30<2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $2{n}^{2}-30<2.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{n}^{2}-30 & <2 \\\\ 2{n}^{2} & <32 \\\\ {n}^{2} & <16 \\\\ \\sqrt{{n}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{16} \\\\ |n| & <4 \\\\ -4<n & <4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe natural numbers that are solutions to the inequality above are $1,2,3.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA={1,2,3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cfaa5b9d30900903e28e1bba97790ae61bb22126fc0e2fa27da8250a38beaca9"} {"question" "q-181794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "N"] ["math" "{1,2,3}"] ["math" "{N}_{0}"] ["math" "{\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{1,2,3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in {R}^{-}:3{x}^{2}\\le 27}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the negative real numbers that satisfy the inequality $3{x}^{2}\\le 27.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2} & \\le 27 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\le \\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & \\le 3 \\\\ -3\\le x & \\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe negative real numbers that are solutions to the inequality above are $x\\in [-3,0).$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA=[-3,0).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathaca