on/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the positive real numbers and zero that satisfy the inequality $9{x}^{2}+4\\le 4.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+4 & \\le 4 \\\\ 9{x}^{2} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution to the inequality above that is in ${R}_{0}^{+}$ is $x=0.$ Therefore, $A={0}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181803" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cfaa5b9d30900903e28e1bba97790ae61bb22126fc0e2fa27da8250a38beaca9"} {"question" "q-181803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R"] ["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{R}^{+}"] ["math" "{R}_{0}^{+}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14e395d2afc1c8d2c339c9242720a47e6a8cee171e52d54122fb638"} {"question" "q-181803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{0}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2f78a8fb14