\mathbb{N}: 5n - 2 \\leq 21 \\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13143.json" "file_sha256" "417f5793d876ca927d4bbab68405e8cbdd8e28a0d09f5d953bfdcf77b4a5b489"} {"question" "e-13143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $5n - 2 \\leq 21.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n-2 & \\le 21 \\\\ 5n & \\le 23 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{23}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $1,2,3,4.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{1,2,3,4\\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13143.json" "file_sha256" "417f5793d876ca927d4bbab68405e8cbdd8e28a0d09f5d953bfdcf77b4a5b489"} {"question" "e-13176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "List the elements of the set $A = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}: x^2 - 9 \\lt 0\\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13176.json" "file_sha256" "db2b8a6d43c34f007d1540c27ea6d045feadfc562205ea9a133721b1dc620ef7"} {"question" "e-13176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $x^2 - 9 < 0.$\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <9 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & <3 \\\\ -3<x & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $0,\\pm1,\\pm2.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{ 0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13176.json" "file_sha256" "db2b8a6d43c34f007d1540c27ea6d045feadfc562205ea9a133721b1dc620ef7"} {"question" "e-13178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "List the elements of the set $A=\\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}: |k-1| \\leq 4 \\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13178.json" "file_sha256" "840e4c163842386ec31c61ce817cb6c1fdaa1b6362a0484a64af1f808ac70376"} {"question" "e-13178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $|k-1| \\leq 4.$ So, we first need to solve for $k{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|k-1|\\le 4 \\\\ -4\\le k-1\\le 4 \\\\ -3\\le k\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5.$ \n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,4,5 \\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13178.json" "file_sha256" "840e4c163842386ec31c61ce817cb6c1fdaa1b6362a0484a64af1f808ac70376"} {"question" "e-13179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "List the elements of the set $A = \\left\\{ x\\in \\mathbb R \\: :\\:  \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0  \\right\\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13179.json" "file_sha256" "28e60783d566095214eeb0df16b09bf10b0897d93581b25abd8291115857dc79"} {"question" "e-13179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{2} & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in\\mathbb Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA= \\{0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13179.json" "file_sha256" "28e60783d566095214eeb0df16b09bf10b0897d93581b25abd8291115857dc79"}] "usage" {"e-13179" [] "q-181185" [] "q-181143" [] "e-13176" [] "q-181117" [] "e-13143" [] "e-13178" []} "basis" 1309 "retractions" [[17592186198697 :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A = {x ∈ R: \\mid 2x + 5|= 13}$?"] [17592186198700 :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A = {x ∈ Q: \\sin (2πx) = 0}$?"] [17592186198703 :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A = {x ∈ R: \\cos (2x) = 1}$?"] [17592186198077 :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\{n \\in \\mathbb{N}: 5n - 2 \\leq 21 \\}$."] [17592186198077 :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality\n\n$$\n5n - 2 \\leq 21\n$$\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5n - 2 & \\le 21 \\\\ 5n & \\le 23 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{23}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $1,2,3,4$. Therefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{1,2,3,4\\}\n$$"] [17592186198087 :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}: x^2 - 9 \\lt 0\\}$."] [17592186198087 :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $x^2 - 9 < 0$.\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x{:}$\n$x^{2} - 9\\begin{vmatrix}< 0 \\\\ x^{2}\\end{vmatrix}< 9; \\sqrt{x^{2}} \\mid < \\sqrt{9}; \\mid x \\mid \\mid < 3; - 3 < x \\mid < 3$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $0,\\pm1,\\pm2$. Therefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}\n$$"] [17592186198088 :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A=\\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}: \\mid k-1 \\mid \\leq 4 \\}$."] [17592186198088 :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality\n\n$$\n\\mid k-1 \\mid \\leq 4\n$$\n\nSo, we first need to solve for $k{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mid k - 1 \\mid \\le 4; - 4 \\le k - 1 \\le 4; - 3 \\le k \\le 5\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5$.\n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,4,5 \\}\n$$"] [17592186198089 :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\left\\{x\\in \\mathbb R \\::\\: \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0 \\right\\}$."] [17592186198089 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{πx}{2} &= nπ \\\\\nx &= 2n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n\nSubstituting different values of $n$, we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\, \\pm 2,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\nA= \\{0,\\, \\pm 2,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\\}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186195133 17592186195134 17592186195135 17592186195136 17592186195137 17592186195172 17592186195173 17592186195174 17592186195175 17592186195176 17592186195195 17592186195196 17592186195197 17592186195198 17592186195199] "immutable_fields" [[17592186195132 :answer-field/correct] [17592186195132 :answer-field/id] [17592186195132 :answer-field/key] [17592186195132 :answer-field/type] [17592186195171 :answer-field/correct] [17592186195171 :answer-field/id] [17592186195171 :answer-field/key] [17592186195171 :answer-field/type] [17592186195194 :answer-field/correct] [17592186195194 :answer-field/id] [17592186195194 :answer-field/key] [17592186195194 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
